PN,31801
SC,0001
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FAfter four consecutive months of
OL,6,Ftemperatures reaching 35C or higher,
OL,7,Fincluding two separate heatwaves that
OL,8,Fsaw highs of 38C, this week marks a
OL,9,Fturning point.
OL,11,FFresher conditions are expected, with
OL,12,Frain and even thunderstorms possible
OL,13,Fin some parts of the UK.
OL,15,FBut does this mean its officially the
OL,16,Fend of summer and what weather can we
OL,17,Fexpect?
OL,19,FIs there rain forecast?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31802
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FSome places had notable rain at the
OL,6,Fweekend including a huge area of
OL,7,Fnorthern England. Parts of Scotland
OL,8,Fand Northern Ireland had had rain on
OL,9,Fand off in recent weeks.
OL,11,FMany of these areas have more rain
OL,12,Fforecast today and many days this week
OL,13,Foffering some relief in the drier
OL,14,Fareas of northern England and Wales.
OL,16,FMuch of the south of England and
OL,17,Fsouthern Wales will stay dry again
OL,18,Fwith some showery bursts of rain from
OL,19,FThursday onwards.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FThe showers and longer downpours will
OL,6,Fcrop up almost anywhere - with an
OL,7,Fincreased chance of heavier bursts and
OL,8,Fthunder.
OL,10,FSome areas of the south will still not
OL,11,Freceive enough rain to end the drought
OL,12,Fconditions.
OL,14,FParts of the south-east haven't
OL,15,Frecorded any rain since mid June.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31804
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FIf the rain is heavy and intense
OL,6,Fduring thundery downpours it will
OL,7,Fstruggle to infiltrate into the ground
OL,8,Fwhich has been baked and hardened by
OL,9,Fweeks of unbroken sunshine and a
OL,10,Fprolonged, exceptional dry few months.
OL,12,FThis will create more surface water in
OL,13,Fplaces - but remains very much needed.
OL,15,FHow about the temperatures - will it
OL,16,Fturn cooler?
OL,18,FAfter hot conditions in many areas
OL,19,Fsince late May - a switch in air mass
OL,20,Fthis week will mean a shock to the
OL,21,Fsystem for many.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31805
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FA northerly air direction will allow
OL,6,Ftemperatures to lower for all of us.
OL,7,FParts of the south-east will see highs
OL,8,Fof 27-28C into a new week and it'll
OL,9,Ffeel muggy - more so with any cloud
OL,10,Fcover.
OL,12,FIn much of the south and south-east
OL,13,Ftemperatures will slowly slide, with
OL,14,F26C on Tuesday, 24C on Wednesday and
OL,15,FThursday and only 21-22C on Friday.
OL,17,FWe've adjusted to much higher
OL,18,Ftemperatures in recent months so it
OL,19,Fwill feel significantly cooler - or
OL,20,Feven colder.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31806
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FAway from the south-east, through the
OL,6,Fsouth-west, Midlands and East Anglia
OL,7,Fand parts of south Wales - expect
OL,8,Ftemperatures just a couple of degrees
OL,9,Flower with 19-21C by Friday.
OL,11,FScotland, Northern Ireland and
OL,12,Fnorthern England will be around 16-19C
OL,13,Fto start the week before sliding to a
OL,14,Fmaximum of 16C towards the weekend.
OL,16,FHow about beyond this week?
OL,18,FHigh pressure returns by the end of
OL,19,Fnext weekend with drier conditions set
OL,20,Fto return - but it'll be a "cooler
OL,21,Fhigh" this time.
OL,26,@|D@\OU}D@EO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/10
