PN,31807
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FThere'll be sunny skies into the start
OL,6,Fof next week but temperatures will
OL,7,Fremain a little lower with much cooler
OL,8,Fand in places chillier nights.
OL,10,FThe weather situation remains more
OL,11,Faligned with changeable theme as
OL,12,FAugust continues as systems move in
OL,13,Ffrom the mid Atlantic.
OL,15,FSubscribe for free to our weekly
OL,16,Fnewsletter for exclusive and original
OL,17,Fcoverage from ITV Wales, sent direct
OL,18,Fto your inbox every Saturday morning.
OL,20,FIs that it for this summer?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31808
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FOur weather in the UK can be fickle.
OL,6,FWe have had some very warm Septembers
OL,7,Fwith a notable record breaking
OL,8,Fheatwave of temperatures in excess of
OL,9,F30C in 2023.
OL,11,FThere's an on going view that the
OL,12,Fweather gets better just as school
OL,13,Fstarts again - and more often than
OL,14,Fnot, high pressure tends to return,
OL,15,Fbringing settled and fine conditions.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31809
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FThe long range forecast from the Met
OL,6,FOffice indicates signs of settled
OL,7,Fweather and warmth as we move through
OL,8,FSeptember - more so towards the
OL,9,Fequinox (when days and nights become
OL,10,Fnearer equal in length).
OL,12,FBrief warmer or hotter spells can't be
OL,13,Fruled out but the trend is for a shift
OL,14,Fafter recent months.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31810
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787014066
OL,3,CIs this the end of our heatwave summer?
OL,5,FThe Met Office longer range forecast
OL,6,Fsuggests a statistically warmer than
OL,7,Faverage August and September - but
OL,8,Fbare in mind the context of more than
OL,9,F30 days of over 30C this summer - it
OL,10,Fmight not feel quite like that given
OL,11,Fwhat we've become used to.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/10
